.TH ROFI-CLIPBOARD 1 "rofi-hub 0.2.1" "rofi-hub" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rofi-clipboard \- pick an entry from cliphist and copy it again
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rofi-clipboard
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rofi-clipboard
lists the entries reported by
.BR "cliphist list"
and, on Enter, decodes the selected entry and pipes it to
.BR wl-copy .
Only the list index is carried in the Rofi row id, so clipboard contents
cannot break the dmenu metadata protocol.
.PP
Both
.B cliphist
and
.B wl-copy
must be present in
.BR PATH .
The command fails cleanly, with a dependency hint, when either is missing or
when the history is empty.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ROFI_BIN
Rofi executable. Defaults to
.BR rofi .
.TP
.B ROFI_CONFIG
Explicit Rofi configuration file.
.TP
.B ROFI_THEME
Theme override. Otherwise
.I ~/.config/rofi/clipboard.rasi
and the system data directories are searched.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, cancel, or an empty history. Non-zero when a dependency is
missing or a subprocess fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rofi-hub (1),
.BR rofi (1),
.BR cliphist (1),
.BR wl-copy (1)
